{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a stitch task (#5148) from an automated work queue. The task is to implement `cmd/dirname` version, help, and unknown option handling per srd016-dirname requirements R4.1-R4.3. Specifically:\n   - R1: Add `--version` flag that prints version information to stdout and exits 0\n   - R2: Add `--help` flag that prints usage information to stdout and exits 0\n   - R3: Ensure unknown options print error to stderr and exit non-zero\n   - Add corresponding differential test cases\n   - Files to modify: `cmd/dirname/main.go` and `cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go`\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go Unix utils project: Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU reference binary (`gdirname`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - GNU coreutils convention for --version and --help output format\n   - NormalizeFunc pattern for handling expected stdout/stderr differences between Go and GNU binaries\n   - `discardStdout` normalizer pattern for --help/--version tests (stdout text differs but exit code must match)\n   - `normalizeBinaryName` pattern to normalize binary names in error messages\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all files\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Write all code before running build/test commands\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd016-dirname.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements. R4.1-R4.3 are in the \"Differential testing\" section. The task maps these to version/help/unknown-option implementation.\n     - Key: R3.2 says \"Must exit 1 when called with no arguments\" and R4.3 says \"Tests must verify error output and exit code when no arguments are given.\"\n\n   - **cmd/dirname/main.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Current implementation handles -z/--zero, --, and basic unknown option detection\n     - Missing --version and --help handling\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd016-dirname.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"fmt\"\n     \t\"os\"\n     \t\"strings\"\n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n     \tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     \targs := os.Args[1:]\n     \tnulDelimited := false\n     \tfor len(args) > 0 {\n     \t\tswitch args[0] {\n     \t\tcase \"-z\", \"--zero\":\n     \t\t\tnulDelimited = true\n     \t\t\targs = args[1:]\n     \t\tcase \"--\":\n     \t\t\targs = args[1:]\n     \t\t\tgoto done\n     \t\tdefault:\n     \t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\") && len(args[0]) > 1 {\n     \t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"dirname: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n     \t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\tgoto done\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     done:\n     \tif len(args) == 0 {\n     \t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"dirname: missing operand\")\n     \t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'dirname --help' for more information.\")\n     \t\tos.Exit(1)\n     \t}\n     \tdelim := byte('\\n')\n     \tif nulDelimited { delim = 0 }\n     \tfor _, arg := range args {\n     \t\tresult := dirname(arg)\n     \t\t_, err := fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%s%c\", result, delim)\n     \t\tif err != nil { os.Exit(1) }\n     \t}\n     }\n     \n     func dirname(path string) string {\n     \tfor len(path) > 1 && path[len(path)-1] == '/' { path = path[:len(path)-1] }\n     \tif path == \"/\" { return \"/\" }\n     \ti := strings.LastIndex(path, \"/\")\n     \tif i < 0 { return \".\" }\n     \tdir := path[:i]\n     \tfor len(dir) > 1 && dir[len(dir)-1] == '/' { dir = dir[:len(dir)-1] }\n     \tif dir == \"\" { return \"/\" }\n     \treturn dir\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Has 16 test cases covering core dirname functionality\n     - Uses `normalizeBinaryName` with regex `(?:/\\S+/)?g?dirname`\n     - Missing --help, --version, and unknown option test cases\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"os/exec\"\n     \t\"regexp\"\n     \t\"testing\"\n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n     )\n     \n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n     \tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n     \trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gdirname\")\n     \tif err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary gdirname not found\") }\n     \tbinaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?dirname`)\n     \tnormalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n     \t\treturn binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"dirname\"))\n     \t})\n     \ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n     \t\t{Name: \"simple_path\", Args: []string{\"/usr/bin/sort\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"no_directory\", Args: []string{\"stdio.h\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"root_path\", Args: []string{\"/\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"trailing_slashes\", Args: []string{\"/usr/bin/\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"dot_path\", Args: []string{\".\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"dotdot_path\", Args: []string{\"..\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"nested_path\", Args: []string{\"a/b/c\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"all_slashes\", Args: []string{\"///\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"multiple_args\", Args: []string{\"dir1/file\", \"dir2/file\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"multiple_args_mixed\", Args: []string{\"/usr/bin/sort\", \"stdio.h\", \"/\", \"a/b/c\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"nul_delimited\", Args: []string{\"-z\", \"/usr/bin/sort\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"nul_delimited_multiple\", Args: []string{\"-z\", \"/usr/bin/sort\", \"stdio.h\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"nul_delimited_long_flag\", Args: []string{\"--zero\", \"/usr/bin/sort\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"end_of_options_with_help\", Args: []string{\"--\", \"--help\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"end_of_options_with_dash_z\", Args: []string{\"--\", \"-z\"}},\n     \t\t{Name: \"no_args_error\", Args: []string{}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName}},\n     \t}\n     \ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/basename/main.go** (reference pattern, not to be modified)\n     - Shows the established pattern for --help and --version in this project\n     - `helpText` const with full usage text\n     - `versionText` const: `basename (go-unix-utils) dev\\n`\n     - --help prints to stdout and exits 0\n     - --version prints to stdout and exits 0\n     - Error format: `unrecognized option '%s'`\n\n   - **cmd/basename/basename_test.go** (reference pattern, not to be modified)\n     - Shows pattern for testing --help/--version: uses `discardStdout` normalizer\n     - `discardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })`\n     - Help test: `{Name: \"help\", Args: []string{\"--help\"}, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout}}`\n     - Version test: `{Name: \"version\", Args: []string{\"--version\"}, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout}}`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was in the research/planning phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified what needs to be added to main.go: `helpText` const, `versionText` const, and `--help`/`--version` cases in the flag parsing switch\n   - Identified what needs to be added to dirname_test.go: `discardStdout` normalizer, test cases for --help, --version, and unknown option\n   - Established the pattern to follow from cmd/basename (the closest sibling utility)\n   - The unknown option handling already parti